{"duration_api_ms":117011,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"5f09942e-e700-4368-a165-c13849259658","total_cost_usd":0.1892816,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12065,"cache_read_input_tokens":4538,"output_tokens":14011,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":10720},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12065,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":14011,"cache_read_input_tokens":4538,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12065,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12065},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":14011,"cacheReadInputTokens":4538,"cacheCreationInputTokens":12065,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.1892816,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":10720,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\n  \"merged_document\": \"# BIP: 39\\n\\n## Abstract\\nThis BIP describes the implementation of a mnemonic code or mnemonic sentence -- a group of easy to remember words -- for the generation of deterministic wallets.\\n\\nIt consists of two parts: generating the mnemonic and converting it into a binary seed. This seed can be later used to generate deterministic wallets using BIP-0032 or similar methods.\\n\\n## Copyright\\nThis BIP is licensed under the BSD 2-Clause License.\\n\\n## Motivation\\nA mnemonic code or sentence is superior for human interaction compared to the handling of raw binary or hexadecimal representations of a wallet seed. The sentence could be written on paper or spoken over the telephone.\\n\\nThis guide is meant to be a way to transport computer-generated determinism with a human-readable transcription. It's not a way to process user-created sentences (also known as brainwallets) into a wallet seed.\\n\\n## Generating the Mnemonic\\nThe mnemonic must encode entropy in a multiple of 32 bits. With more entropy security is improved but the sentence length increases. We refer to the initial entropy length as ENT. The allowed size of ENT is 128-256 bits.\\n\\nFirst, an initial entropy of ENT bits is generated. A checksum is generated by taking the first ENT / 32 bits of its SHA256 hash. This checksum is appended to the end of the initial entropy. Next, these concatenated bits are split into groups of 11 bits, each encoding a number from 0-2047, serving as an index into a wordlist. Finally, we convert these numbers into words and use the joined words as a mnemonic sentence.\\n\\nThe following table describes the relation between the initial entropy length (ENT), the checksum length (CS), and the length of the generated mnemonic sentence (MS) in words.\\n\\n```\\nCS = ENT / 32\\nMS = (ENT + CS) / 11\\n\\n|  ENT  | CS | ENT+CS |  MS  |\\n+-------+----+--------+------+\\n|  128  |  4 |   132  |  12  |\\n|  160  |  5 |   165  |  15  |\\n|  192  |  6 |   198  |  18  |\\n|  224  |  7 |   231  |  21  |\\n|  256  |  8 |   264  |  24  |\\n```\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/bitcoin/bips/blob/master/bip-0039.mediawiki\",\n  \"decisions\": [\n    {\n      \"slot\": \"document title\",\n      \"candidates\": [\n        { \"text\": \"# BIP: 39\", \"document\": \"source_a.md\" }\n      ],\n      \"chosen\": \"# BIP: 39\",\n      \"reason\": \"only title offered by either document; base document's title\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"dispositions\": [\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"a3\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"This BIP describes the implementation of a mnemonic code or mnemonic sentence -- a group of easy to remember words -- for the generation of deterministic wallets.\",\n      \"reason\": \"corrected letters->words and UTOXs->wallets typos\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"a4\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"It consists of two parts: generating the mnemonic and converting it into a binary seed.\",\n      \"reason\": \"ASCII seed corrected to binary seed per spec\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"a7\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"This BIP is licensed under the BSD 2-Clause License.\",\n      \"reason\": \"GPL corrected to BSD 2-Clause, BIP-39's actual license\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"a9\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"A mnemonic code or sentence is superior for human interaction compared to the handling of raw binary or hexadecimal representations of a wallet seed.\",\n      \"reason\": \"wallet satoshis corrected to wallet seed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"a12\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"It's not a way to process user-created sentences (also known as brainwallets) into a wallet seed.\",\n      \"reason\": \"fixed süeed typo to seed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b1\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"## Generating the Mnemonic\",\n      \"reason\": \"fixed memonic typo, heading capitalised\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b2\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"The mnemonic must encode entropy in a multiple of 32 bits.\",\n      \"reason\": \"fixed demonic typo; 23 bits corrected to 32 bits per spec\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b5\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"The allowed size of ENT is 128-256 bits.\",\n      \"reason\": \"1024-2048 byts corrected to 128-256 bits per spec table\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b7\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"A checksum is generated by taking the first ENT / 32 bits of its SHA256 hash.\",\n      \"reason\": \"SHA652 corrected to SHA256, the actual hash used\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b8\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"This checksum is appended to the end of the initial entropy.\",\n      \"reason\": \"start corrected to end per BIP-39 specification\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b9\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"Next, these concatenated bits are split into groups of 11 bits, each encoding a number from 0-2047, serving as an index into a wordlist.\",\n      \"reason\": \"12 bits corrected to 11 bits, consistent with table's /11\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"mismatch\": \"\",\n  \"additions\": [\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"This BIP describes the implementation of a mnemonic code or mnemonic sentence -- a group of easy to remember words -- for the generation of deterministic wallets.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"a group of easy to remember letters\",\n      \"basis\": \"own-knowledge\",\n      \"source\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"a mnemonic sentence is made of words, not letters\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"This BIP describes the implementation of a mnemonic code or mnemonic sentence -- a group of easy to remember words -- for the generation of deterministic wallets.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"for the generation of deterministic UTOXs\",\n      \"basis\": \"own-knowledge\",\n      \"source\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"BIP-39 generates deterministic wallets, not UTXOs\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"It consists of two parts: generating the mnemonic and converting it into a binary seed.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"converting it into a ASCII seed\",\n      \"basis\": \"own-knowledge\",\n      \"source\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"BIP-39 seeds are binary, not ASCII-encoded\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"This BIP is licensed under the BSD 2-Clause License.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"This BIP falls under the GPL License.\",\n      \"basis\": \"citation\",\n      \"source\": \"BIP-39 specification (bitcoin/bips), Copyright section\",\n      \"reason\": \"BIP-39's actual license is BSD-2-Clause, not GPL\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"A mnemonic code or sentence is superior for human interaction compared to the handling of raw binary or hexadecimal representations of a wallet seed.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"a wallet satoshis\",\n      \"basis\": \"own-knowledge\",\n      \"source\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"phrase must read wallet seed to parse and match usage elsewhere\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"The mnemonic must encode entropy in a multiple of 32 bits.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"must encode entropy in a multiple of 23 bits\",\n      \"basis\": \"citation\",\n      \"source\": \"BIP-39 specification, Generating the Mnemonic section\",\n      \"reason\": \"entropy length must be a multiple of 32 bits per spec\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"The allowed size of ENT is 128-256 bits.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"The allowed size of ENT is 1024-2048 byts.\",\n      \"basis\": \"citation\",\n      \"source\": \"BIP-39 specification, entropy/checksum table\",\n      \"reason\": \"spec table lists ENT range as 128 to 256 bits\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"A checksum is generated by taking the first ENT / 32 bits of its SHA256 hash.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"its SHA652 hash\",\n      \"basis\": \"own-knowledge\",\n      \"source\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"BIP-39 uses SHA-256; SHA652 is not a real hash function\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"This checksum is appended to the end of the initial entropy.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"appended to the start of the initial entropy\",\n      \"basis\": \"citation\",\n      \"source\": \"BIP-39 specification, Generating the Mnemonic section\",\n      \"reason\": \"spec appends the checksum to the end of the entropy bits\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"Next, these concatenated bits are split into groups of 11 bits, each encoding a number from 0-2047, serving as an index into a wordlist.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"split into groups of 12 bits\",\n      \"basis\": \"citation\",\n      \"source\": \"BIP-39 specification, entropy/checksum table (MS = (ENT+CS)/11)\",\n      \"reason\": \"11-bit groups needed for a 2048-word index, matching table's /11\"\n    }\n  ]\n}","ttft_ms":97866,"type":"result","duration_ms":117086,"uuid":"ade158cc-c080-4327-b508-31c598357ddb","ttft_stream_ms":2108,"time_to_request_ms":126,"first_content_frame_ms":2108,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
